#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   10074193
#=GF RT   Mutagenic analysis of the 3' cis-acting elements of the rubella virus
#=GF RT   genome.
#=GF RA   Chen MH, Frey TK
#=GF RL   J Virol 1999;73:3386-3403.
#=GF CC   This family represents a cis-acting element found at the 3' UTR in the
#=GF CC   rubella virus. This family contains three conserved step loop structures.
#=GF CC   Pfam:PF00262 (CAL) which is known to bind calcium in most eukaryotic
#=GF CC   cells, is able to specifically bind to the first stem loop. CAL binding is
#=GF CC   thought to be related to viral pathogenesis and in particular arthritis
#=GF CC   which is a occurs frequently in rubella infections in adults and is
#=GF CC   independent of viral viability. All stem loop structures are thought to be
#=GF CC   important for efficient viral replication and deletion of stem loop three
#=GF CC   is known to be lethal [1].
#=GF WK   Rubella_virus_3'_cis-acting_element
#=GF SQ   25

